[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SYS-VAL-001
VERSION: 1
TITLE: Reject invalid calculations
STATEMENT: >>>
If a calculation request contains an operand that is not a valid string
number, or asks for a division by zero, then the service **shall** respond
with an error response that contains an error code and no result.
<<<
KIND: functional
STATUS: draft
PRIORITY: high
SAFETY: QM
RELEASE: 1.0.0
VERIFICATION: test
VERIF_LEVELS: system
TAGS: validation, api
SOURCE: Stakeholder request, 2026-11-18
OWNER: msforenter090
CREATED: 2026-11-18T00:00:00Z
RATIONALE: >>>
A client must never receive a result it could mistake for a correct one.
An error code lets the client react to the reason without parsing text.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
- The error response format, the error codes and the exact validation rules
  are defined at software level. See child requirements REQ-API-002,
  REQ-VAL-001 and REQ-VAL-002.
<<<
